1
00:04:32,500 --> 00:04:38,500
He can save us all.

2
00:09:05,000 --> 00:09:11,000
Elysium is a science fiction, action, drama film directed by Neill Blomkamp.

3
00:13:37,500 --> 00:13:43,500
In the year 2159, two classes of people exist: the very wealthy who live on a pristine man-made
space station called Elysium, and the rest, who live on an overpopulated, ruined Earth.

4
00:18:10,000 --> 00:18:16,000
Secretary Rhodes, a hard line government official, will stop at nothing to enforce
anti-immigration laws and preserve the luxurious lifestyle of the citizens of Elysium.

5
00:22:42,500 --> 00:22:48,500
That doesn’t stop the people of Earth from trying
to get in, by any means they can.

6
00:27:15,000 --> 00:27:21,000
When unlucky Max is backed into a corner, he agrees to take on a daunting mission that, if
successful, will not only save his life, but could bring equality to these polarized worlds.

7
00:31:47,500 --> 00:31:53,500
Max, played by Matt Damon.

8
00:36:20,000 --> 00:36:26,000
Delacourt, played by Jodie Foster.

9
00:40:52,500 --> 00:40:58,500
Kruger, played by Sharlto Copley.

10
00:45:25,000 --> 00:45:31,000
Julio, played by Diego Luna.

11
00:49:57,500 --> 00:50:03,500
Spider, played by Wagner Moura.

12
00:54:30,000 --> 00:54:36,000
Frey, played by Alice Braga.

13
00:59:02,500 --> 00:59:08,500
Elysium is a 2013 American dystopian science fiction action film
written, co-produced, and directed by Neill Blomkamp.

14
01:03:35,000 --> 01:03:41,000
It was Blomkamp's second directorial effort.

15
01:08:07,500 --> 01:08:13,500
The film stars Matt Damon and Jodie Foster alongside Sharlto Copley,
Alice Braga, Diego Luna, Wagner Moura, and William Fichtner.

16
01:12:40,000 --> 01:12:46,000
The film takes place on both a ravaged Earth and a
luxurious artificial world called Elysium.

17
01:17:12,500 --> 01:17:18,500
The film itself offers deliberate social commentary that explores political and sociological themes such as immigration,
overpopulation, transhumanism, health care, worker exploitation, the justice system, technology, and social class issues.

18
01:21:45,000 --> 01:21:51,000
The film was released on August 9, 2013, by Sony Pictures Releasing through the
TriStar Pictures label, in both conventional and IMAX Digital theaters.

19
01:26:17,500 --> 01:26:23,500
It received positive reviews, but critics considered it to be
disappointing after Blomkamp's first film, District 9.

20
01:30:50,000 --> 01:30:56,000
With a budget of $115 million, Elysium was TriStar's most expensive film.

21
01:35:22,500 --> 01:35:28,500
It grossed $286.1 million worldwide.

22
01:39:55,000 --> 01:40:01,000
The film explores themes of future, capitalism,
dystopia, space station, class conflict.

23
01:44:27,500 --> 01:44:33,500
The tone is emotional and thought_provoking and intense.
